{
  "name": "weather_dimming_census",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a713's full vanilla WeatherDef census: every weather Ludeon ships, pinned to the exact fraction it dims by, including the non-weathers that must stay at 0. The expected dimming values track the SHIPPED preset strength (CelestialSettingsMath.Presets.Cinematic.WeatherDimming, currently 0.20), because that is what WeatherDimmingSettings.MaxDimming defaults to in a fresh install. They are exact on purpose \u2014 pinning the whole ladder is this scenario's job \u2014 which means a preset change invalidates every one of them. To recompute: dimming = opacity * lerp(0.6*M, M, max(rain,snow,sand)/1.6), and purkinje = PurkinjeFactor(skyGlow * (1 - dimming)). If you only care which side of zero a reading falls on, use weather_dimming_skyless.json's wide bands instead of copying this file's exactness.",
